  "description": "Works to a tree in a conservation area:\rT1 Robinia - Remove tree & stump (poor condition). Plant replacement tree.\rT2 Robinia - Remove tree & stump (poor condition). Plant replacement tree.\rT3 Leyland Cypress - Remove tree & stump adjacent to side of property. Plant replacement tree.\rT4 Lime - Remove deadwood (exempt), crown lift to 5m\rT5 Lime - Remove deadwood (exempt), crown lift to 5m\rT6 Lime - Remove deadwood (exempt)\rT7 Lime - Remove tree & stump (basal decay, stem bleeding). Plant replacement tree.\rT8 Sycamore - Reduce height by approx. 3m and radial spread by approximately1.5m (Squirrel damage). Approximately 15m height and 5.5m radial spread on completion of pruning\rG12 Leyland Cypress group x 5 - Reduce height by a maximum of 6m to form cohesive group (also removing dead material in upper crown, roadside) Approximately 13m height on completion.\rH15 Leyland Cypress hedge - Reduce height by approximately 3m (retaining sufficient live growth to maintain tree health). Approximately 10m height on completion \rT21 Bay - Prune to ensure 1m-2m clearance from building",
